<title>LEBANON: Bank of Lebanon weekly CDs raise 11 bln pounds.</title>
<headline>Bank of Lebanon weekly CDs raise 11 bln pounds.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Lebanon issued certificates of deposit dated October 4 to commercial banks worth 11 billion Lebanese pounds compared with one billion last week.</p>
<p>The Bank sold 45-day CDs worth three billion pounds carrying interest of 12.75 percent and 60-day CDs worth eight billion pounds at 13.50 percent.</p>
<p>Last week it sold only 60-day CDs worth one billion.</p>
<p>Interest rates were unchanged for the fourth week running.</p>
<p>($1 = 1,558.25 Lebanese pounds)</p>
<p>- Beirut editorial (9611) 864148 645456 353078 602057</p>
